Pangolin software and model
---------------------------

Pangopup is a new Rust implementation intended to reproduce and extend the
behavior of the GPL-3.0 Pangolin project:

  Project: Pangolin
  Author: Tony Zeng
  Source: https://github.com/tkzeng/Pangolin
  Version inspected: 1.0.2
  License: GNU General Public License version 3
  Citation: Zeng T, Li YI. Predicting RNA splicing from DNA sequence using
            Pangolin. Genome Biology 23, 103 (2022).

Pangopup distributes a converted ONNX representation of the Pangolin 1.0.2
checkpoint set in its separately versioned `runtime-grch38-v1` release. That
release retains the upstream license and notices, identifies the exact source
commit and checkpoint hashes, identifies Pangopup's conversion, and provides
the corresponding Pangolin and Pangopup preferred source archives. The thin
container image does not embed the model; `pangopup sync` installs it from the
authenticated runtime release.

Pangolin precomputed scores dataset
-----------------------------------

Pangopup is designed to transform and query the following separately licensed
dataset:

  Title: Pangolin precomputed scores
  Creators: Nils Wagner and Aleksandr Neverov
  Publisher: Zenodo
  DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.15649338
  Source: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15649338
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The Pangopup index is a transformed representation of the source per-gene TSV
files. Pangopup may reorder, validate, index, and losslessly pack their numeric
fields for exact lookup. It does not change the source scores.

Distributed index bundles must retain this notice, identify the exact source
archive checksum, describe the transformation, and state whether further
changes were made.

HGNC gene naming source
-----------------------

Pangopup reads the following separately licensed file to name the gene an
Ensembl accession belongs to:

  Title: HGNC complete set, monthly release 2026-09-04
  Publisher: HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee (HGNC), EMBL-EBI
  File: hgnc_complete_set_2026-09-04.tsv
  Source: https://storage.googleapis.com/public-download-files/hgnc/archive/archive/monthly/tsv/
  Size: 16903161 bytes
  SHA-256: 6f43d6ff43aa9fdfa5fb2f20a20a7cace66e6e02e2a0dcf19d9b726e2e248d20
  License: Creative Commons Public Domain (CC0)
  License text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

HGNC publishes no upstream checksum file for this release. Pangopup pins the
dated release member by byte count and its own computed digest. The naming
source is never embedded in an index bundle, a runtime profile or the
container image. It installs through the offline asset path and reaches no
network at scoring time or at service start.

GENCODE annotation
------------------

The Pangopup domain mask is derived from the following annotation:

  Title: GENCODE human release 38 comprehensive annotation
  Creators: The GENCODE consortium
  Publisher: EMBL-EBI
  File: gencode.v38.annotation.gtf.gz
  Source: https://ftp.ebi.ac.uk/pub/databases/gencode/Gencode_human/release_38/
  Terms: GENCODE names no separate licence and refers to the EMBL-EBI terms of use
  Terms text: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/about/terms-of-use

The mask records the annotated gene domains the model scores against. It
carries no GENCODE sequence and no GENCODE transcript payload.

